---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const siteUrl = "https://zentype.jonathanrreed.com";
const subprocessorUrl = `${siteUrl}/subprocessors/`;
---

<PageLayout
	title="Zen Typer keeps the public site stack small."
	seo={{
		title: "Zen Typer Subprocessor Disclosure",
		description: "Subprocessor disclosure for Zen Typer, including Cloudflare Pages hosting and browser-local typing practice storage.",
		canonical: subprocessorUrl,
		keywords: [
			"Zen Typer subprocessors",
			"typing app subprocessors",
			"local storage typing app",
			"Zen Typer privacy",
		],
		breadcrumbItems: [
			{ name: "Mindful typing test", url: `${siteUrl}/` },
			{ name: "Zen Typer subprocessors", url: subprocessorUrl },
		],
	}}
>
	<p slot="lede" class="prose-lede">
		Zen Typer has no accounts. Typing sessions, drafts, settings, and stats stay in browser storage on the device you use, so there is exactly one company in the chain: the host.
	</p>

	<section>
		<h2>Current infrastructure</h2>
		<p>
			Zen Typer is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare may process routine request metadata, such as IP address, user agent, request time, and security signals, to deliver and protect the site.
		</p>
		<p>
			There are no user accounts, payments, cloud sync, hosted draft storage, analytics, or shared workspaces. Nothing you type is transmitted unless you export it yourself and put the file somewhere.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Future changes</h2>
		<p>
			If Zen Typer ever adds accounts, sync, analytics, or payments, this page changes before those services see any traffic. There are no plans to.
		</p>
		<p>
			Questions about subprocessors or data handling go through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. This disclosure was last updated on September 4, 2026.
		</p>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
